    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build succeeded, meaning the OpenAPI generator produced the `selfLink` field on `OwnerDto` and MapStruct compiled the new mapping expression.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was to return `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` + the owner id. The test (`AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink`) creates an owner and reads `$.selfLink` back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so the field needs to appear on every owner response \u2014 GET, POST-create, and the list page.\n\nTwo changes, both at the DTO/mapping layer so all responders benefit automatically:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` (readOnly string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits `OwnerDto.setSelfLink(...)`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `selfLink` with the expression `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()`, matching the existing pattern for the other derived fields (`displayName`, `fiscalYear`, etc.).\n\nBecause `toOwnerDto` is used by `RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, and the list mapper, the self-link is populated consistently across all owner responses without touching any pipeline YAML or function class.",
